Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:
> Jan Rocho wrote:
> [ problems finding Xaw lib ]
> 
> Such problems with Xaw had been mentioned earlier, and I too failed
> to compile it on by box as delivered.  Since many seem to have that
> problem that might be considered to be fixed in the standard delivery.
> 
> To solve the problem I just added the lib path to the link options in
> src/Makefile:
> 
> WINX11LIB = -L/usr/X11/lib -lXaw -lXmu -lXext -lXt -lX11
>              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
> 
> Change it to X11R6 in your case.

Note that (a more general fix for) this _is_ documented; from
win/X11/Install.X11:

  If your X11 include files and libraries are not installed in a standard
  place (i.e. /usr/include/X11 and /usr/lib respectively) you will need to
  prepend an appropriate -I<idirectory> parameter to CFLAGS and a
  -L<ldirectory> parameter to LFLAGS, setting <?directory> to the place to
  find the include and library files for X11.

I don't think that the DevTeam should be expected to directly cater
for every possible non-standard place various Unices might put them.

